{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: numeric payload fields don't tolerate string-typed values**

```dart
int? intOf(String key) => payload?[key] is int ? payload![key] as int : null;
```

`intOf` (and `text` above it) only accept the exact JSON type. Gateways and proxies in front of codex-shaped backends frequently serialize numeric fields as strings (`{"resets_in_seconds": "2280562"}`, `"resets_at": "1792439371"`). In that shape the advertised reset is silently dropped (`resetsInSeconds`/`resetsAt` null) and the message degrades to "Try again later." even though the server told us exactly when it resets — the one thing this PR set out to surface.

Cheap hardening on the degrade path:

```dart
int? intOf(String key) {
  final value = payload?[key];
  if (value is int) return value;
  if (value is String) return int.tryParse(value);
  return null;
}
```

Same tolerance for `resets_at` follows automatically via `intOf('resets_at')`. Unknown shapes still degrade exactly as before.
